{"t":55.46,"code":0,"d":{"duration_api_ms":18177,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d1c923b0-7dcb-47d6-9c5c-14e747e56851","total_cost_usd":0.028863,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3495,"cache_read_input_tokens":25330,"output_tokens":1233,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":40},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":606,"cache_read_input_tokens":6468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":263},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":1233,"cacheReadInputTokens":25330,"cacheCreationInputTokens":3495,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.028863,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":40,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":3495,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Mostly yes through debt, but with limits. The bond market is open but getting more expensive, and Pellham in particular looks constrained.**\n\n- **Market access:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp. They were 130bp in Q1 and 135bp in Q2. Even so, Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\" in Q3, so the market is open at a higher price (docs `utility-credit`, series `utility_spreads`).\n- **Norvane:** Its 2027 spending is planned up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2. The C$1.1B bond already covers a large part of that tender, so Norvane looks financeable through debt.\n- **Pellham:** It plans 2027 spending up 18%, with a C$900M transformer tender due to award in Q1 2027 (doc `utility-tenders`). Pellham's C$2.4B equity offering was pulled on 14 October. It then said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 tender (doc `pellham-offering`). The pulled equity raise and the order cut suggest Pellham cannot fund the full plan from debt alone without stretching its balance sheet. Pellham may be able to borrow, but it is choosing to cut orders.\n- **Gaps in the evidence:** I found no data on total debt maturities, leverage or credit ratings, or on Pellham's debt capacity.\n- **Equity market:** n6 concluded that equity is mostly shut at the scale needed (n6.r1).\n\n**Conclusion:** Norvane can fund its plan in the bond market. For Pellham, debt access seems to exist but is not enough to carry the original plan. That is why it is trimming orders and resizing its tender. If spreads keep widening, the pressure on both would grow.","ttft_ms":1473,"type":"result","duration_ms":49661,"uuid":"e8769f07-d361-4271-9e6c-48abd5b8b2cf","ttft_stream_ms":1040,"time_to_request_ms":63,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":13,